// markdownlint-cli2 configuration for `just lint`. Scope is the *rendered* markdown —
// the docs site sources, the READMEs and the ADRs (rendered by GitHub rather than Hugo);
// CLAUDE.md files are Claude-facing and unrendered, so they stay out for the same reason
// they are exempt from the explicit-issue-link rule.
//
// Rules run at their strict defaults except:
// - MD013 (line length): off. The ~100-column wrap is a soft convention kept by review, and
//   issue-link syntax (`[#N]({{< param BookRepo >}}/issues/N)`) legitimately pushes source
//   lines far past any cap while rendering short — enforcing a source-line limit would force
//   mid-link wraps or per-line disables on dozens of correct lines.
// - MD060 (table column style): off. Tables here deliberately pair compact delimiter rows
//   (`|---|`) with spaced content cells; MD060 wants one style for both.
// - MD025: the Hugo pages carry a front-matter `title` *and* an H1 (the Flink page shape);
//   front_matter_title "" stops the front matter from counting as a second top-level heading.
// - MD052 shortcut_syntax: on. The ADRs' issue-link idiom is the shortcut reference —
//   `[#N]` in prose, `[#N]: url` in a definition block — and MD052's default checks only
//   full and collapsed references, so a missing definition rendered as literal `[#N]` with
//   every check green: seven shipped that way, introduced five times in eight days with no
//   natural fix ever observed (#1035). The override below turns it back off for
//   docs/content only, where micromark cannot parse a Hugo shortcode destination and
//   reports every such link as unresolved (measured: 435 false positives in 39 files).
//   `overrides` (in the pinned 0.23.2) keeps this in one file; a nested
//   .markdownlint.jsonc was probed first and *replaces* this config object — MD013
//   silently re-enabled across every docs page — so do not reach for one.
//
// MD051 (in-page anchor fragments resolve) is a default-on rule this file exists to keep:
// Hugo's build validates `relref` cross-page links but never `[text](#anchor)` fragments.
{
  "config": {
    "MD013": false,
    "MD025": { "front_matter_title": "" },
    "MD052": { "shortcut_syntax": true },
    "MD060": false
  },
  "overrides": [
    {
      "filter": ["docs/content/**/*.md"],
      "config": { "MD052": { "shortcut_syntax": false } },
      "combine": "merge"
    }
  ],
  "globs": [
    "docs/content/**/*.md",
    "docs/adr/**/*.md",
    "README.md",
    "flink-*/README.md",
    "opentofu/README.md"
  ]
}
